;;-*-Lisp-*-
(in-package goal)

;; name: editable-player.gc
;; name in dgo: editable-player
;; dgos: ENGINE, GAME

;; DECOMP BEGINS

;; og:preserve-this R2 enabler (issue 571's UX successor): transcribed verbatim
;; from jakx's own editable-player.o decode (scoped decode of this object,
;; *editable-menu-context* at disasm.gc:6666-6670; jak3's landed twin carries the
;; identical pair at its own editable-player.gc:3156,3158). default-menu.gc's real
;; menu-respond-to-pause body (landed same rung) calls debug-menu-context-send-msg
;; on *editable-menu-context* on every 'menu-mode branch and in its else arm, so
;; without this definition set-master-mode's first invocation dereferences an
;; unbound symbol and crashes goal-0 (the #115 class). This object (498) builds
;; ahead of default-menu (504), so the definition exists before default-menu needs
;; it.
;;
;; og:preserve-this debug-segment guard (runtime-falsified, tip smoke): the
;; *debug-menu-context* type's own new method (goal_src/jakx/engine/debug/
;; menu.gc:92) allocates its font sub-object on the 'debug kheap, and that
;; kheap only exists when the C++ runtime's DebugSegment flag is set
;; (game/kernel/jakx/kmachine.cpp:296-302, "if no debug, we make the
;; kheapinfo structure NULL so GOAL knows not to use it"); the same flag is
;; what *debug-segment* itself reads back as (game/kernel/jakx/kscheme.cpp:
;; 1924-1929), so *debug-segment* is NOT unconditionally true the way an
;; earlier campaign note assumed, only true when booted with -debug. A
;; default (non-debug) boot leaves kdebugheap.offset at 0, and this line was
;; the first place in the whole campaign to attempt a 'debug allocation from
;; an object's own top-level (as opposed to from a function body invoked
;; later, well after boot); the crash was a near-null read at offset 0x10
;; inside that allocation chain, rip in unmapped code, matching exactly.
;; Guarded the same way debug.gc and debug-sphere.gc already guard their own
;; debug-segment-only top-level content ((when *debug-segment* ...)); on a
;; -debug boot this constructs the real context exactly as before, and on a
;; default boot it binds #f instead of crashing goal-0.
(define *editable-menu-context* (when *debug-segment* (new 'debug 'debug-menu-context)))
(when *editable-menu-context*
  (set! (-> *editable-menu-context* joypad-number) 1)
  )

